                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "74ecfeec-5024-42f6-bb25-7bfb969d2bde",
                        "entry_id": "f550c6df-877d-32a2-b565-4d9d2b04138a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "пи́жмах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0adb1a2-402c-352a-b42d-3856ed47e1b5",
                        "entry_id": "f550c6df-877d-32a2-b565-4d9d2b04138a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. многолетнее травянистое растение семейства астровые, с очерёдными, перисто-рассечёнными или перисто-лопастными листьями и соцветиями в форме корзинок, собранных в единое щитковидное соцветие (Tanacetum)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ba287ba-98f0-43e1-a5db-bf1310387d3f",
                                "sense_id": "b0adb1a2-402c-352a-b42d-3856ed47e1b5",
                                "text": "Улица впадала в замечательно просторный пустырь, весь зараставший в июле пижмой… — жёлтой, как небо, когда солнце рассекает золотыми вёслами тонкие пёристые облака…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d2b7f0a-caca-3ccd-a33e-1cc99d574270",
                        "entry_id": "f550c6df-877d-32a2-b565-4d9d2b04138a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свежие или высушенные части этого растения, используемые для лекарственных целей и в кулинарии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86b015a1-f2df-4139-bb69-969e0bd5faf4",
                                "sense_id": "7d2b7f0a-caca-3ccd-a33e-1cc99d574270",
                                "text": "А модной в среде роллеров минеральной воде «Перье» я предпочитаю спиртовой настой пижмы."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4cc87980-8c6c-4dac-a077-985338395992",
                        "source_entry_id": "f550c6df-877d-32a2-b565-4d9d2b04138a",
                        "source_sense_description": "растение",
                        "target_lang_word": "tansy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tansy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae2b65da-a97c-3343-b57d-921e9e9a5301",
                                        "entry_id": "e0863c11-d071-3ba6-bb5e-664e648f8445",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A herbaceous plant with yellow flowers, of the genus Tanacetum, especially Tanacetum vulgare."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5349570-5376-41aa-a882-87a30fab66b2",
                                                "sense_id": "ae2b65da-a97c-3343-b57d-921e9e9a5301",
                                                "text": "The sunny afternoon was there, like another land. By the path grew tansy and little trees."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9feb0f7-4e97-49f5-b6ff-d28a93f49695",
                                                "sense_id": "ae2b65da-a97c-3343-b57d-921e9e9a5301",
                                                "text": "Various measures were taken to avoid it, most popular being the suspension of certain herbs and tree branches over the doorways of dwellings and stables. Commonly used greenery were tansy, honesty, garlic, St. John's Wort, mountain ash, roadside verbena."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7df7fae-a7ed-3d13-96e4-45e5a02bff8c",
                                        "entry_id": "e0863c11-d071-3ba6-bb5e-664e648f8445",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dish common in the seventeenth century, made of eggs, sugar, rose water, cream, and the juice of herbs (including tansy), baked with butter in a shallow dish. \\\"Originally flavoured with tansy, but by Pepys's time generally having spinach as its predominant flavouring.\\"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5cee285-b7a2-4068-96b1-fe66fda55baf",
                                                "sense_id": "e7df7fae-a7ed-3d13-96e4-45e5a02bff8c",
                                                "text": "I had a pretty dinner for them; viz., a brace of stewed carps, six roasted chickens, and a jowle of salmon, hot, for the first course; a tanzy and two neats' tongues, and cheese the second; and were very merry all the afternoon, talking and singing and piping upon the flageolette."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
